Develop a circuit that converts a 4-bit binary input into a 4-bit Gray code output. The module employs a three-stage pipelining technique to ensure that the conversion process is executed systematically, with each stage handling specific bit manipulations to produce the Gray code representation, where each successive value differs by only one bit from the previous value.
