Design a logic circuit that computes an output based on a combination of inputs. The output X is determined by the state of the signals A1_N and A2_N. If both A1_N and A2_N are LOW, X is set HIGH (1). If A1_N is LOW while A2_N is HIGH, X takes the value of input B2. Conversely, if A2_N is LOW while A1_N is HIGH, X takes the value of input B1. If both A1_N and A2_N are HIGH, X is set to LOW (0). This design effectively functions as a conditional output selector based on the status of its inputs.
