description:
Design a modified Johnson counter that utilizes a shift register configuration with n flip-flops, where n is parameterized at 4. The counter operates on the rising edge of a clock signal and has an asynchronous reset input. Upon reset, the output and internal state are initialized to zero. On each clock cycle, the counter shifts the most significant bit (MSB) into the least significant bit (LSB) position, effectively creating a unique sequence of output states that is characteristic of Johnson counters. The output presents the current state of the counter, providing a straightforward means of digital state representation.
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input rst,
  output reg [n-1:0] out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input clk,
  input rst,
  output reg [n-1:0] out
);parameter n = 4; // number of output signals

reg [n-1:0] q;

always @(posedge clk, posedge rst) begin
  if (rst) begin
    q <= 0;
    out <= 0;
  end
  else begin
    q <= {q[n-2:0], q[n-1]};
    out <= q;
  end
end

endmodule

