description:
Design a 4-bit adder module that computes the sum of two 4-bit inputs, A and B. The output, X, is a 5-bit value that includes a carry bit. If the sum of A and B does not exceed 15 (i.e., the maximum value representable by 4 bits), the output X is a zero-extended 5-bit result. If the sum exceeds 15, X directly reflects the computed 5-bit sum, accommodating the carry bit.
module top_module(
    input [3:0] A,
    input [3:0] B,
    output reg [4:0] X  // Change output type to reg
);

code:
module top_module(
    input [3:0] A,
    input [3:0] B,
    output reg [4:0] X  // Change output type to reg
);wire [4:0] sum;

    assign sum = A + B;

    always @(*) begin
        if (sum <= 15) begin
            X = {1'b0, sum};
        end else begin
            X = sum;
        end
    end

endmodule

